## Description
The is_unsurfaced_due closure at engine/resume.rs:47-51 guards against re-stamping by checking f.surfaced_at.is_none(). The FactStore::stamp_surfaced implementation at store/facts.rs:484-486 also has an 'AND surfaced_at IS NULL' guard. Both gates are correct but neither is covered by a test that calls resume_context twice on the same due fact. A second call should leave surfaced_at unchanged (same timestamp); if either guard drifts, re-stamping would update the timestamp, breaking monotonicity of the surfacing record.

